  "homepage": "https://github.com/zakirhossen23/railcall-jira-module",
  "tests_url": "https://github.com/zakirhossen23/railcall-jira-module/tree/main/edudzi-jira/test",
  "description": "Governed Jira Cloud automation for RailCall — thirty-one commands covering the full issue lifecycle, comments, labels, watchers, components, versions, issue links, changelogs, plus multi-step composites, over the Jira REST API v3 (Basic Auth with an Atlassian API token stored in the RailCall vault; egress allowlisted to *.atlassian.net and *.jira.com).\n\nWHO IT'S FOR\nEngineering teams who want an AI agent to run day-to-day Jira hygiene — triage, follow-ups, status moves, assignment, attachments, comments, labels, watchers — without raw credentials or unreviewed writes. Every mutating command is dry-run-first: RailCall previews the exact payload and requires explicit approval; each approved run yields a signed receipt.\n\nREAD (low risk)\n- getIssue — one issue by key/id (summary, status, assignee, fields).\n- searchIssues — JQL via POST /search/jql; token pagination, no total.\n- listIssueTypes — instance-wide types.\n- getTransitions — valid transitions + ids for an issue.\n- listProjects — accessible projects.\n- getProjectIssueTypes — valid types for one project (createmeta).\n- getChangelog — full change history for an issue.\n- getComments — all comments on an issue.\n- getWatchers — list watchers on an issue.\n- getComponents — project components.\n- getVersions — project versions.\n\nWRITE (medium risk, approval-gated)\n- createIssue — create; plain text auto-converted to ADF.\n- updateIssue — edit summary/description.\n- addComment — comment (ADF).\n- updateComment — edit an existing comment.\n- transitionIssue — move by transition id.\n- assignUser — by accountId or email.\n- attachFile — upload text/base64.\n- linkIssues — create a link between two issues.\n- addLabels — add labels to an issue.\n- addWatcher — add a watcher to an issue.\n- createComponent — create a project component.\n- createVersion — create a project version.\n\nCOMPOSITES (several API calls under ONE approval)\n- triageIssue — fetch context, comment, optional transition.\n- resolveWithNote — closing note + transition together.\n- cloneIssue — copy an issue into a new one.\n- bulkTransitionFromJql — transition every JQL match (per-issue outcomes).\n\nDESTRUCTIVE (high risk, approval-gated)\n- deleteIssue — delete, optionally subtasks.\n- deleteComment — delete a comment.\n- removeIssueLink — remove a link between issues.\n- removeWatcher — remove a watcher from an issue.\n\nQUICK START\n1. Token: id.atlassian.com → Security → API tokens.\n2. Studio → Integrations: add JIRA_DOMAIN, JIRA_EMAIL, JIRA_API_TOKEN.\n3. Install: railcall market install edudzi/jira\n4. Try: jira_listProjects → jira_createIssue → jira_getIssue\n\nERROR BEHAVIOR\n- Every HTTP >= 400 raises with field-level errors surfaced verbatim.\n- No write is ever retried — one shot, fail loud.\n- Issue types are project-specific; use getProjectIssueTypes to discover valid types.\n- Issue types are project-specific (Product Discovery accepts only \"Issue\").\n\ncontest:2026Q3",
